===Etymology===
A transliteration from {{bor|en|cmn|-}} {{zh-l|揚子}}, [[Wade-Giles]] romanization: ''Yang²-tze³''.

The Chinese character name corresponding to 'Yangtze River', {{zh-l|揚子江}}, was borrowed from an old name for the part of the Yangtze River near [[Yangzhou]].

The folk etymology that it means "Son of the Ocean" derives from the homophonic [[misnomer]] {{m|zh|[[洋]][[子]][[江]]}} which was apparently given to {{w|Matteo Ricci}}, whose posthumously-published journals popularized the name in Europe as {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|Iansu}} and {{m|la|Iansuchian}}.

